From: Mehmet Salih <salihmehmet497@gmail.com>
Subject: PCI: quirk EN7523 (MT7622-style) root ports: drop the bogus 8 GiB BAR0

The MediaTek/Airoha root ports on EN7523 (14c3:0810 and 14c3:0811) expose a
BAR0 that sizes to 0x200000000. The core cannot handle it ("can't handle
BAR larger than 4GB", then "alignment must not be zero"), the resource stays
IORESOURCE_UNSET, and pci_enable_bridge() fails with -EINVAL ("Error
enabling bridge (-22), continuing"). The bridge therefore never gets
PCI_COMMAND_MEMORY set (it reads 0x0144 out of reset).

Real-hardware effect on the Zyxel EX3501-T0: the MT7916 behind it enumerates
and its registers can be read, but every MCU message times out ("Failed to
get patch semaphore", probe -11). Setting bit 1 of the root port's command
register by hand and rebinding mt7915e makes the firmware load and the MCU
answer immediately (verified 2026-09-25). Zero the BAR0 resource on these
root ports so the bridge enables normally.

--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -5598,6 +5598,26 @@
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_HUAWEI, 0xa22b, quirk_no_flr_snet);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_MEDIATEK, 0x0616, quirk_no_flr);
 
+/*
+ * Airoha EN7523 (MT7622-style) PCIe root ports report an 8 GiB BAR0 that the
+ * core cannot size or assign; the unassigned resource then makes
+ * pci_enable_bridge() fail so the bridge never enables memory decoding and
+ * endpoints behind it cannot DMA. The BAR is not used for anything: drop it.
+ */
+static void quirk_airoha_en7523_root_port_bar(struct pci_dev *dev)
+{
+	struct resource *res = &dev->resource[0];
+
+	if (!res->flags)
+		return;
+
+	pci_info(dev, "dropping unusable root port BAR 0 %pR\n", res);
+	res->flags = 0;
+	res->start = res->end = 0;
+}
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_MEDIATEK, 0x0810, quirk_airoha_en7523_root_port_bar);
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_MEDIATEK, 0x0811, quirk_airoha_en7523_root_port_bar);
+
 /* FLR may cause the SolidRun SNET DPU (rev 0x1) to hang */
 static void quirk_no_flr_snet(struct pci_dev *dev)
 {
